import texture_shapes.dl

to complete UI image {a pointer to UI image:image} in {a pointer to UI view:view} with resource {a pointer:resource} sized {integer:width} by {integer:height} at status {integer:status}:
    require condition (image's status = 0) reporting "An image completed more than once"
    require condition ((status = 1) or (status = 2)) reporting "An image returned an invalid completion status"
    if status = 1:
        require condition (((resource != (0 as a pointer)) and (width > 0)) and (height > 0)) reporting "A decoded image has no texture"
    else:
        require condition (((resource = (0 as a pointer)) and (width = 0)) and (height = 0)) reporting "A failed image retained a texture"
    set image's texture to @intrinsic("construct", UI texture, resource, width, height)
    set image's status to status
    set view's images changed to true
    set view's damaged to true
    @intrinsic("call pointer", view's driver's wake, nothing, view)

to get the cached UI [image] from {string:path} in {a pointer to UI view:view}:
    set image to view's images
    loop while image != @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI image):
        if image's path = path:
            return image
        set image to image's next
    return image

to get UI [image] from {string:path} in {a pointer to UI view:view}:
    require condition (path's length > 0) reporting "A UI image requires an asset path"
    set image to the cached UI image from path in view
    if image = @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI image):
        set record to a new UI image
        set record's path to path
        set record's next to view's images
        set image to storage for one slot initialized with record
        set view's images to image
    # Construction can return a view by value. Start callbacks only after its
    # observer binds its final address, just like the shared input/lifetime path.
    if (image's requested = false) and (view's observer != @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI observer)):
        set image's requested to true
        @intrinsic("call pointer", view's driver's open image, nothing, image, view)
    return image

to start UI [image] loads in {a pointer to UI view:view}:
    set image to view's images
    loop while image != @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI image):
        if image's requested = false:
            set image's requested to true
            @intrinsic("call pointer", view's driver's open image, nothing, image, view)
        set image to image's next

to release UI images in {a pointer to UI view:view}:
    set image to view's images
    loop while image != @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI image):
        set next to image's next
        if image's requested:
            @intrinsic("call pointer", view's driver's close image, nothing, image, view)
        destroy the value at image
        deallocate image
        set image to next
    set view's images to @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI image)

to draw UI image {a pointer to UI image:image} in {UI bounds:box} rounded by {floating-point number:radius} fitting {integer:fit} on {UI frame:frame}:
    require condition ((fit >= 0) and (fit <= 2)) reporting "Unknown image fit"
    if (image's status != 1) or ((box's width <= 0.0) or (box's height <= 0.0)):
        return nothing
    set texture to image's texture
    set sample to UI box at 0 0 sized 1 1
    set target to box
    if fit = 0:
        set scale to the minimum of (box's width / texture's width) and (box's height / texture's height)
        set target's width to texture's width * scale
        set target's height to texture's height * scale
        set target's x to box's x + (box's width - target's width) / 2.0
        set target's y to box's y + (box's height - target's height) / 2.0
    if fit = 1:
        set scale to the maximum of (box's width / texture's width) and (box's height / texture's height)
        set sample's width to box's width / (texture's width * scale)
        set sample's height to box's height / (texture's height * scale)
        set sample's x to (1.0 - sample's width) / 2.0
        set sample's y to (1.0 - sample's height) / 2.0
    draw UI texture texture in target rounded by radius sampling sample in (UI ink 255 255 255) with opacity 255 on frame
